From: Deividas Nastajus <16858119+dns54@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 05:27:53 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 22/25] FatPkg/EnhancedFatDxe: Stop at a looping directory
 cluster chain

FatPhysicalDirSize() follows a directory's cluster chain until it
ends, and only stops early at a free or reserved cluster. A chain that
points back into itself never ends: a FAT volume whose root directory
cluster points to itself hangs the firmware in a loop that does no I/O
as soon as the volume is mounted, for example when a USB stick is
plugged in before boot.

A chain can't have more clusters than the volume, so treat a longer
one as corrupt, like the free and reserved cases.

Signed-off-by: Deividas Nastajus <16858119+dns54@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 FatPkg/EnhancedFatDxe/FileSpace.c | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/FatPkg/EnhancedFatDxe/FileSpace.c b/FatPkg/EnhancedFatDxe/FileSpace.c
index 909d4980d2..acd5360bce 100644
--- a/FatPkg/EnhancedFatDxe/FileSpace.c
+++ b/FatPkg/EnhancedFatDxe/FileSpace.c
@@ -657,6 +657,7 @@ FatPhysicalDirSize (
   )
 {
   UINTN  Size;
+  UINTN  Remaining;
 
   ASSERT_VOLUME_LOCKED (Volume);
   //
@@ -664,12 +665,16 @@ FatPhysicalDirSize (
   //
   Size = 0;
   //
+  // A chain can't be longer than the volume's cluster count; a longer one loops.
+  //
+  Remaining = Volume->MaxCluster;
+  //
   // N.B. ".." directories on some media do not contain a starting
   // cluster.  In the case of "." or ".." we don't need the size anyway.
   //
   if (Cluster != 0) {
     while (!FAT_END_OF_FAT_CHAIN (Cluster)) {
-      if ((Cluster == FAT_CLUSTER_FREE) || (Cluster >= FAT_CLUSTER_SPECIAL)) {
+      if ((Cluster == FAT_CLUSTER_FREE) || (Cluster >= FAT_CLUSTER_SPECIAL) || (Remaining-- == 0)) {
         DEBUG (
           (DEBUG_INIT | DEBUG_ERROR,
            "FATDirSize: cluster chain corrupt\n")
